---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

---

<Layout
  title="Verdict is uninstalled"
  description="What happened to your data when you removed Verdict."
>
  <h1>Verdict is uninstalled</h1>
  <p>
    It is gone from your browser, along with everything it stored. That was all of it: your
    check history, the cached review data, and your preferences never lived anywhere else.
  </p>

  <h2>Your history is deleted</h2>
  <p>
    Verdict kept your history on your own machine and never had a copy. There is no account to
    close and no server to write to, so removing the extension removed the data with it. If you
    wanted to keep it, an export from the options page was the way, and that page is gone now
    too.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you reinstall, Verdict starts empty. You can import nothing, because there was never
    anywhere to import from.
  </p>

  <h2>If something was wrong</h2>
  <p>
    Reports that looked wrong are worth telling us about, and so are pages Verdict read badly.
    The <a href="/status">status page</a> shows whether extraction is currently working on each
    site, which is often the answer.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can <a href="/install">install it again</a> at any time.
  </p>
</Layout>
